ith a gunmetal and brass rim. One primary subject, at most one supporting object; no pile of props. Use restrained enamel colour suited to the specific subject and nationality. Keep the central silhouette bold and the rim free of tiny ornamental clutter.\n\nRequirements:\n- Take the frame, outline and overall form from the style anchor images, not from a fixed family form; the size, transparency, margin and readability requirements here still apply.\n- Flags and ribbons use invented colours, never a real country's flag, unless the brief names that country.\n- The subject is large: it fills most of the emblem and may overlap its frame, never a small figure inside a wide empty plaque.\n- A strong central symbol that supports the focus's story, readable contrast at 100x88 pixels.\n- Real transparent background around the emblem: no backdrop behind it.\n- Leave a small empty margin around the emblem.\n\nReference images, in the order attached:\n1. style anchor: match its painting style, palette and level of detail\nThe style anchor images were chosen for this image. Match their form, framing, materials and palette; the vanilla form described under Requirements applies only where they do not show one.\n\nAvoid: text; letters or numbers; watermark or signature; a drawn checkerboard pattern; a square backdrop behind the subject.\n\nProduce exactly one image.\n",
